<title>SOUTH KOREA: KEPCO shares soar on foreign buying.</title>
<headline>KEPCO shares soar on foreign buying.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of South Korea's electricity monopoly Korea Electric Power Corp (KEPCO) gained 1,200 won to 29,800 in early afternoon trading on Wednesday on buying by foreign investors, brokers said.  </p>
<p>Brokers said foreign investors placed buying orders for about 300,000 KEPCO shares.</p>
<p>&quot;KEPCO has emerged as a new darling among foreigners as their investment limits for other blue chips like Samsung Electronics and POSCO were hit,&quot; said Na Min-ho, a broker at Daishin Securities.</p>
<p>About 18 million KEPCO shares are still available for foreign buying.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
